# 23. Common Proxy Mistakes

## Mistake 1: Choosing Only by Price

The cheapest proxy may not provide the stability or geographic coverage required.

## Mistake 2: Assuming Residential Means Trusted

Residential classification does not guarantee good reputation.

## Mistake 3: Rotating IPs Constantly

Frequent rotation may make some account sessions less consistent.

## Mistake 4: Ignoring Browser Configuration

A proxy does not replace browser-profile management.

## Mistake 5: Testing Only Connectivity

A proxy that connects successfully may still perform poorly for the target workflow.

## Mistake 6: Changing Everything at Once

If you change the proxy, browser, account, and workflow simultaneously, troubleshooting becomes difficult.

## Mistake 7: Scaling Before Testing

Deploying an untested proxy configuration across dozens or hundreds of sessions can multiply problems.

