# 28. What Proxy Quality Cannot Guarantee

Even a high-quality proxy cannot guarantee:

* No CAPTCHA
* No security checks
* No account verification
* No detection
* Successful access to every website
* Permanent IP reputation
* That a website will trust the traffic

Security systems are controlled by the destination website.

A proxy provider cannot determine how a website evaluates its traffic.

---

# 29. Frequently Asked Questions

## Can a bad proxy cause more CAPTCHAs?

It can contribute to increased scrutiny if the IP has characteristics or reputation that the website considers unusual.

## Are residential proxies always better?

No. The appropriate proxy depends on the use case, website, location, reliability, and other factors.

## Are mobile proxies CAPTCHA-free?

No. Mobile networks can still receive CAPTCHAs and other forms of verification.

## Does changing the IP always solve CAPTCHA problems?

No. Other factors such as browser fingerprints, cookies, account activity, and behavior can remain unchanged.

## Should every account have a different proxy?

Not every workflow requires this, but separating accounts and network environments can make multi-account infrastructure easier to manage and troubleshoot.

## Is proxy rotation always better?

No. Some workflows benefit from stability rather than constant IP changes.

## How can I compare proxies?

Test them under controlled conditions and record connectivity, latency, stability, geographic accuracy, workflow reliability, and CAPTCHA frequency.

## Can MarketerBrowser manage proxies?

Yes. MarketerBrowser includes proxy configuration as part of its browser-profile management workflow.

