# Conclusion

Proxy quality is one piece of the CAPTCHA puzzle.

An IP address can influence how traffic is evaluated, but it is only one layer among many:

```text id="7j2v8p"
IP / Proxy
     +
Browser Fingerprint
     +
Cookies
     +
Account
     +
Session
     +
Behavior
     |
     v
Risk Assessment
```

This is why switching proxies randomly is rarely a complete solution.

For legitimate browser automation, research, testing, and multi-account workflows, a better approach is to select appropriate proxy infrastructure, maintain stable browser environments, test systematically, and monitor results over time.

The key principle is simple:

> **A good proxy is not simply an IP that connects. It is network infrastructure that is reliable, appropriate for the workflow, and predictable enough to manage.**
